From 49e89aea343f9f76402c348bdd801f7a12661ce0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:44:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] translation pane: every page, every locale, every
 candidate with its provenance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner's rulings of 2026-11-18 on per-block translation feedback, pane side
(the data side is litlfred/cat-harness-tools#2432):

1. The 🌐 pane mounts on every page, source-language pages included. It lists
   every locale's current translation of the block's strings and its status
   (official / adjudicated / proposed / agent / MT / missing / stale), from the
   catalogue's strings projection (folio-translation-strings/v1). A site with
   no review.json says so plainly and shows what the page itself says.
2. ✎ Fix translation offers every candidate, the current one included, with
   its provenance: source and version, date, author, issue, stale, glossary
   and round-trip QA, and the unofficial default pick. The sidecar is still
   read directly when no projection is published.
3. The text says what the workflow does: a collaborator's choice becomes the
   translation; anyone else's is kept as a proposal. A source page gets a
   fix per locale.

Tested by cat-harness-tools test/block-translation-review.e2e.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
